From: Gilly1970 <gilroyscott@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 1 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: reject empty TCP payload in the LRO path

The hardware aggregation path accepts a TCP segment whose data offset is at
or beyond the received length, i.e. a segment that carries no payload (a
pure ACK).  Feeding it to the aggregation engine builds a GRO packet around
invalid payload data.

Reject those segments before aggregation.

Signed-off-by: Gilly1970 <gilroyscott@hotmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -968,7 +968,7 @@ static struct sk_buff *airoha_qdma_rx_gro(struct airoha_queue *q,
 		return NULL;
 
 	data_off = th_off + (th->doff << 2);
-	if (len < data_off)
+	if (len <= data_off)
 		return NULL;
 
 	tcp_win = FIELD_GET(QDMA_ETH_RXMSG_TCP_WIN_MASK, msg3);
